{
  "rules": [
    "Uptrend underestimation: when the last 5–10 days show a clear rebound/rally, the model systematically underprices the next 10–30 days. Apply an upward level shift that grows with horizon (small at 1–5d, larger at 15–30d).",
    "Horizon-dependent negative bias: errors are modest in the first week but become increasingly negative beyond ~day 10, especially in rising regimes. Use a linear ramp correction (e.g., add progressively more from day 10 to day 30).",
    "Lag after regime change: following a local bottom and subsequent breakout, the forecast path reacts too slowly (trend lag). Increase slope/gradient of the forecast for ~1–2 weeks after a reversal signal.",
    "Missed spike magnitude: for strong upside moves in the realized path (late-horizon highs), the model captures direction but not amplitude. Add a volatility/momentum kicker when recent realized volatility or 3–5 day momentum is high.",
    "Over-smoothing/mean-reversion pull: forecasts revert toward the prior mean too aggressively, causing persistent underprediction during sustained climbs. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is above a rising short-term moving average (e.g., 5d > 20d)."
  ]
}
